# Ratchet source bundle — what must never ship in a release
#
# Running the hook suite in this tree exercises the real hooks, which write real
# runtime state into harness/.pipeline/. That state is the authors' test residue:
# command logs, event logs, and escalation records carrying real run tokens and
# target hashes. It is dead weight in a bundle (install.sh never copies
# .pipeline/), but ratchet-update.sh accepts a .zip, so anything left here after
# a test run travels to users. Keep the tree clean instead of remembering to.

harness/.pipeline/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Never, under any circumstances. Credentials must not enter history.
secrets/
*.key

# Session scratch from the device bridge: base64/tar staging, and the holding pen
# this mount needs because it cannot unlink() (mv works, rm does not). Neither is
# repo content, and _transfer/ accumulates multi-hundred-KB tarballs.
_transfer/
_to_delete/
_patched-2026-08-23/
